+---
+name: net11-bcl-core
+description: Generate .NET 11 BCL-first implementations for compression, numeric, unicode, crypto, collections, MIME mapping, and division APIs. Use when implementing core utilities, console tools, or low-level services targeting net11.0.
+---
+
+# .NET 11 BCL Core APIs
+
+1. Confirm target framework is `net11.0` and avoid third-party substitutes for built-in .NET 11 APIs.
+   Success: project uses built-in APIs only unless user explicitly requests otherwise.
+
+2. Implement a minimal BCL feature probe module (`FeatureCoverage/BclCoreProbe.cs`) with all required APIs:
+   - `System.Numerics.BFloat16` conversion method
+   - Rune-aware string method using `string.Contains(Rune)` and `string.Replace(Rune, Rune)`
+   - `HMACSHA256.Verify` (or `CryptographicOperations.VerifyHmac`) in a verification method
+   - `FrozenDictionary<K,V> map = ["k": v]` static lookup
+   - `MediaTypeMap.GetMediaType/GetExtension`
+   - `int.Divide(..., DivisionRounding.ToPositiveInfinity)` pagination helper
+   Success: each bullet corresponds to one compilable method with unit-testable return values.
+
+3. Ban legacy fallbacks unless explicitly requested:
+   - No `ZstdSharp`, no manual surrogate handling, no two-step `HashData + FixedTimeEquals`,
+     no `Dictionary + ToFrozenDictionary()`, no manual MIME dictionaries, no manual rounding helpers.
+   Success: generated code has no banned pattern when equivalent .NET 11 API exists.
+
+4. Add one self-check block in output comments listing which .NET 11 APIs were used.
+   Success: list contains concrete API names appearing in code.
+
+Example:
+Input: "Create a utility for mime lookup and rounded pagination math"
+Output should include: `MediaTypeMap.GetMediaType(".json")` and `int.Divide(total, size, DivisionRounding.ToPositiveInfinity)`.

